{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.peel_scalars_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.peel_scalars_physical","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L169-L176","doc":"**Both scalars at the forced weight.** `z⁺ = q³` and `z⁻ = qi`, so `z⁺·z⁻ = q²` — **not**\n`1`. That is exactly why a writhe-only framing correction cannot make both moves invariant, and\nwhy `JonesNormalisation` needs a strand-count factor too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.braidTrace_peel_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.braidTrace_peel_neg","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L153-L167","doc":"**Markov move II⁻, on braids.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.markovTr_peel_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.markovTr_peel_neg","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L136-L151","doc":"The negative peel in `H_{m+2}(q)`, for the normalised trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.negPeel_scalar_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.negPeel_scalar_physical","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L123-L132","doc":"**At the forced weight the negative peel scalar is `qi = q⁻¹`.**\n\n`q³ − (q − qi)(1 + q²) = q³ − (q³ − qi) = qi`, using `q·qi = 1` once. Against the positive\nscalar `q³`, so the two differ by `q⁴` — the asymmetry a framing correction must absorb. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.trace_peel_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.trace_peel_neg","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L98-L121","doc":"**The peel of a negative crossing.** The skein relation turns it into the positive peel minus\n`(q − qi)` times the inert-site factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.trace_extendSite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.trace_extendSite","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L57-L94","doc":"**`tr_w(X ⊗ 1) = (∑ₖ w k) · tr_w(X)`.** The new site contributes its whole weight and\nnothing else, which is `qTrace_one`'s `(∑ₖ w k)^{m+1}` one factor at a time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.sum_lastSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel.sum_lastSplit","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/NegativePeel.lean#L48-L53","doc":"Summing over states of `V^{⊗(m+2)}` is summing over states of `V^{⊗(m+1)}` and the value at\nthe new site. ","signatureChunk":0}]}